9. The Chain Reaction
Here is what happens when a user enters the minimum set of parameters.

Round 1.

App 12 (N Calculator) consumes target_tail, relative_error. Produces N, recommended_N, monte_carlo_uncertainty.

App 11 (Effective-Null Builder) consumes null_model, support_rule, selection_function, measurement_kernel. Produces effective_null.

App 4 (Scale-Separation Record Calculator) consumes the two scales, their sources, the band. Produces scale_separation_ratio, scale_separation_anchoring_flag.

App 13 (Gap-Score Reporter) consumes observed_data, candidate_gaps, expected_density. Produces gap_score.

App 22 (Numerical Verification Tool) consumes submitted_document, source_list. Produces verification_table.

App 49 (Autofill Library Service) consumes the user's lookup query. Produces the field values.

Round 2.

App 8 (Pipeline Specification Wizard) consumes recommended_N. Produces pipeline_specification, N, alpha, seed.

App 1 (STAG Annotation Editor) consumes scale_separation. Produces annotation_id, derived_display_label, evidential_anchoring_status.

App 2 (STAG Annotation Validator) consumes annotation_id. Produces validation_report.

App 9 (Full-Pipeline Simulator) consumes pipeline_specification and effective_null. Produces observed_statistic, exceedance_probability, monte_carlo_uncertainty.

Round 3.

App 3 (PROV-O Exporter) consumes annotation_id. Produces provo_document.

App 5 (STAG Graph Viewer) consumes annotation_id. Produces graph_rendering.

App 6 (Partition Sensitivity Explorer) consumes annotation_id and alternative_partition. Produces recomputed_record.

App 7 (Revision History Viewer) consumes annotation_id. Produces revision_chain, change_log.

App 10 (Scan-Family Comparator) consumes pipeline_specification and effective_null. Produces critical_value, power.

App 14 (STAG plus Null-Model Combined Workbench) consumes annotation_id, validation_report, pipeline_specification, statistical_gap_result, critical_value, power. Produces dependence_gap_discordance.

Round 4.

App 15 (Journal Submission Checker) consumes submitted_document, annotation_id, pipeline_specification, statistical_gap_result, audit_report. Produces submission_checklist_report.

App 16 (Teaching and Training Sandbox) consumes example_selection, parameter_changes. Produces recomputed_label, recomputed_statistic.

App 20 (Provenance-Aware Annotation Database) consumes annotation_id, provo_document. Produces stored_records.

App 21 (STAG Audit Tool) consumes submitted_document, checklist. Produces audit_report.

Round 5.

App 19 (Reproducibility Deposit Template) consumes author_code, author_data, author_seeds, author_results. Produces deposit_repository.

App 25 through App 44 (the domain registries) consume the user's deposits and the foundation apps. They produce their domain records.

Round 6.

App 23 (Physics Knowledge Library) consumes work_id, stag_annotations, null_model_results, statistical_gap_result, provo_document, audit_report, verification_table, submission_checklist_report, deposit_repository. Produces stored works.

App 46 (Evidence Aggregator) consumes the evidence from App 25, App 26, App 40, App 41, App 42. Produces aggregate_strength.

App 47 (Replication Cost Estimator) consumes the study characteristics, the N Calculator, the Pipeline Specification Wizard, the Effective-Null Builder, the Instrument Provenance Registry, the Replication Tracker. Produces total_cost.

Round 7.

App 45 (Claim Lifecycle Tracker) consumes the claims from App 23, App 25, App 26, App 38, App 40, App 41, App 42, and the evidence from App 46. Produces lifecycle_events.

Round 8.

App 48 (Meta-Science Dashboard) consumes the data from App 23, App 25, App 26, App 38, App 40, App 41, App 42, App 44, App 45, App 46. Produces dashboard_metrics.

Settled. No app's inputs change. The chain reaction stops.

10. The Minimum User Input Set
The user does not need to enter every parameter. The orchestrator fills in the rest. The minimum set the user must enter is:

observed_data. The data.

null_model. The null density.

support_rule. S1, S2, or S3.

scan_family. Adjacent, pair, or fixed.

g_min_value. The minimum gap width.

tail_definition. Greater-than-or-equal or greater-than.

alpha. The nominal level.

And for the domain apps, the user enters the name of the system, the study, the claim, or the concept. The Autofill Library Service (App 49) fills in the rest.

Everything else is either computed by an app or has a default.

