Data flow:

The module registry, parameter registry, and dependency graph are loaded.

The data bus is created.

The apps are started in dependency order.

The user enters parameters.

The orchestrator propagates them through the dependency graph.

Each app recomputes when its inputs are available.

The results are published on the data bus.

The chain reaction continues until it settles.

14. Technology Stack
Recommended for the orchestrator:

Language: Python 3.11+ or Node.js 20+.

Framework: FastAPI (Python) or Express (JS).

Plugin system: importlib (Python) or dynamic import (JS).

Dependency resolution: networkx (Python) or graphlib (JS).

Shared core: the STAG schema library (App 17), the Null-Model Protocol library (App 18), the provenance database (App 20), the authentication layer, the reporting layer.

Web interface: React or Svelte.

GraphQL: Strawberry (Python) or Apollo Server (JS).

